ine","kabul"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"The Abul Fazl Shrine is a Shi'ite Islamic shrine and mosque, located in Murad Khane, Kabul, Afghanistan. The mosque-shrine complex is named in honour of Abu'l-Fazl ibn Mubarak, a Grand Vizier of the 16th-century Mughal emperor Akbar.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Abul Fazl Shrine","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Blue_mosaic_mosque%2C_Kabul.jpg/1280px-Blue_mosaic_mosque%2C_Kabul.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Blue_mosaic_mosque%2C_Kabul.jpg/500px-Blue_mosaic_mosque%2C_Kabul.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Step from Amherst, USA","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blue_mosaic_mosque,_Kabul.jpg"}},{"id":"kabul_afghan_film","areaId":"kabul","name":"Afghan Film","category":"museum","tags":["museums"],"location":{"lat":34.53114,"lng":69.18727},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"kabul_afghan_film","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":130,"wikidataSitelinks":9,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["afghanfilm","kabul"],"hours":{"week":[null,{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Closed Mon; Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Afghan Film also known as Afghan Film Organization (AFO) is Afghanistan's state-run film company, established in 1968. One of its former presidents Sahraa Karimi, who attained a PhD in Cinema from the Academy of Performing Arts in Bratislava, was its first female president.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Afghan Film","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Sbhan_amini_in_afghan_film.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Sbhan_amini_in_afghan_film.jpg","w":1200,"h":2133,"author":"Sbhanamini","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sbhan_amini_in_afghan_film.jpg"}},{"id":"kabul_kabul_hoard","areaId":"kabul","name":"Kabul hoard","category":"monument","tags":["history","art","photo"],"location":{"lat":34.5148,"lng":69.195},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"kabul_kabul_hoard","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":3,"wikiPageviews":280,"wikidataSitelinks":9,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["kabulhoard","kabul"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"morning","summary":"The Kabul hoard, also called the Chaman Hazouri, Chaman Hazouri or Tchamani-i Hazouri hoard, is a coin hoard discovered in the vicinity of Kabul, Afghanistan in 1933. The collection contained numerous Achaemenid coins as well as many Greek coins from the 5th and 4th centuries BCE.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Kabul hoard","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/54/Chaman_Hazouri_coin_type.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/54/Chaman_Hazouri_coin_type.jpg","w":1200,"h":581,"author":"CNG Coins","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chaman_Hazouri_coin_type.jpg"}},{"id":"kabul_ghazi_s